**Updated Thread Architecture (Complete SSL Isolation):**

Each QUIC connection now uses **complete single-thread SSL lifecycle management**:

**1. Main QUIC Thread (`cas_qm_*`) - Complete SSL Lifecycle:**
```c
void *quicMainLoop(void *args) {
    // === SSL CREATION (Thread-local) ===
    QUIC_CONNECTION *conn = quicOpaqueAllocConnection(startUpArgs);
    // - Creates SSL object via SSL_new()
    // - Performs SSL_connect()  
    // - All SSL setup in same thread

    // === START EVENT WATCHER THREAD ===
    pthread_create(&thread, NULL, quicOpaqueEventWatcher, conn);

    // === SSL USAGE (Thread-local) ===
    quicOpaqueIOLoop(conn);  // All SSL_read_ex/SSL_write_ex operations

    // === SSL CLEANUP (Thread-local) ===
    quicExitMainLoop(conn);
    pthread_join(thread, NULL);  // Wait for watcher to exit

    // === SSL DESTRUCTION (Thread-local) ===
    quicOpaqueFreeConnection(conn);
    // - SSL_shutdown()
    // - SSL_free()  
    // - All cleanup in same thread
}
```

**2. Event Watcher Thread (`cas_qs_*`) - Zero SSL Access:**
```c
void *quicOpaqueEventWatcher(void *arg) {
    while (noError) {
        // === PURE SOCKET MONITORING ===
        FD_SET(sock, &readFDs);
        FD_SET(exitSignalSock, &readFDs);
        select(width, &readFDs, NULL, NULL, &conn->quicEventTimeValue);

        if (FD_ISSET(exitSignalSock, &readFDs)) {
            noError = false;  // Exit signal
            continue;
        }

        // === SIGNAL MAIN THREAD ===
        noError = signalQueuePush(&conn->mainQueue, SAIDA_CAS_SIGNAL_TYPE_ON_OPENSSL_SHOULD_READ) &&
                  signalQueuePop(&conn->openSSLEventQueue) == SAIDA_CAS_SIGNAL_TYPE_NEED_OPENSSL_EVENT_FOR_READING;
    }
}
```

**Key Isolation Guarantees:**
- **Single-thread SSL lifecycle**: Create → Use → Destroy all in `cas_qm_*` thread
- **Zero cross-thread SSL access**: Watcher thread never touches SSL objects, fd and struct timeval are updated by the ways like the demo, in  `cas_qm_*` thread 
- **Independent SSL contexts**: Each connection has completely separate SSL state

